ekf_imu.hpp -- IMU/estimator correctness and host-safe failure behavior.

1. Report LiDAR timestamp regression through an exception.
2. Seed gravity from mean acceleration direction at the known physical
   magnitude, with a stable fallback, in both initialization and reset paths.
3. Undistort points against an externally supplied odometry prior instead of IMU
   dead reckoning, when one is installed and the option is on. Deskew error is
   baked into the voxel map at insertion, so it is the one sharpening lever that
   does not touch the estimated trajectory. All of a sweep or none of it: a
   point the prior cannot place is not half-corrected, it is asserted to be at
   the sweep-end pose already. Inert unless enabled.

Every hunk has an in-source `voxelslam_bridge:` rationale. The complete file
delta is generated with `diff -U3` and applied with zero fuzz.

